  "objective": "Selecting and interpreting a control chart: X-bar and R, X-bar and s, individuals and moving range, median, p, np, c and u",
  "secondaryObjectives": [
    "Explaining the aims of SPC and telling common-cause from special-cause variation"
  ],
  "sources": [
    {
      "cite": "NIST/SEMATECH e-Handbook of Statistical Methods, 6.3.2.1 Shewhart X-bar and R and S Control Charts",
      "checkedAt": "2026-11-16",
      "url": "https://itl.nist.gov/div898/handbook/pmc/section3/pmc321.htm",
      "note": "Read through a summarizing fetch 2026-11-16. Relevant text: X-bar chart UCL = x-double-bar + A2 R-bar, center line x-double-bar, LCL = x-double-bar - A2 R-bar; R chart UCL = R-bar D4, center line R-bar, LCL = R-bar D3; A2 = 3/(d2 sqrt(n)). The factor values used (A2 = 0.577, D3 = 0, D4 = 2.114 for subgroups of 5) are the standard table values and were not on the fetched page; the limits in the case (R-bar 3.1 g: 500.2 to 503.8 g, R up to 6.55 g) are computed from them."
    },
    {
      "cite": "NIST/SEMATECH e-Handbook of Statistical Methods, 6.3.2 What are Variables Control Charts? (WECO rules)",
      "checkedAt": "2026-11-16",
      "url": "https://itl.nist.gov/div898/handbook/pmc/section3/pmc32.htm",
      "note": "Read through a summarizing fetch 2026-11-16. Relevant text: the WECO rules, among them '8 Consecutive Points on This Side of Control Line' and '2 Out of the Last 3 Points Below -2 Sigma'; for a point outside the control limits 'we conclude the process has shifted and is unstable'. The page gives no corrective procedure; finding and removing the cause before adjusting is the case's teaching, consistent with the objective."
    },
    {
      "cite": "NIST/SEMATECH e-Handbook of Statistical Methods, 6.3.3.2 Proportions Control Charts",
      "checkedAt": "2026-11-16",
      "url": "https://itl.nist.gov/div898/handbook/pmc/section3/pmc332.htm",
      "note": "Read through a summarizing fetch 2026-11-16. Relevant text: p 'is the fraction defective in a lot or population'; 'the control chart for proportion or fraction nonconforming ... is called the p-chart'. The p-chart limits in the case (p-bar 0.07, n = 5, UCL 0.41) are computed with the usual three-sigma binomial form, which was not on the fetched text."
    }
  ],
  "brief": {
    "situation": "You are the Green Belt on shift at Riverside Foods (fictional). Line 3 fills 500 g bags of rice; every 15 minutes the operator weighs 5 bags. The supervisor charts them on a p chart of bags under 500 g and wants to release pallets P1 to P4 for the 12:00 truck because 'nothing is over the limit'. It is 11:00.",
    "handover": [
      "The hopper was cleaned at 08:50."
    ],
    "howItWorks": [
      "Pick a step from the action list: open or profile something, run a query, a check or a test, change the code or the model, or ship the result. A cell marked with a pencil can be changed by picking a value. Nothing you pick is typed or executed: every step shows an authored result.",
      "Each step takes working minutes, and the clock moves by the minutes it takes. The deadline runs on the same clock.",
      "The console shows what is open, its flags, charts, tables and code, and the result of each step. 'Read the console' reads it aloud, and every chart can be shown as a table.",
      "Shipping is final for this case. Afterwards you record what you found and explain your reasoning."
    ]
  },
